1
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:00,000
A tough cop. A brilliant killer. An unspeakable crime.

2
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Insomnia is a thriller, crime, drama film directed by Christopher Nolan.

3
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Two Los Angeles homicide detectives are dispatched to a northern town where the sun
doesn't set to investigate the methodical murder of a local teen.

4
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Will Dormer, played by Al Pacino.

5
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Walter Finch, played by Robin Williams.

6
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:30,000
Ellie Burr, played by Hilary Swank.

7
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:24,000
Hap Eckhart, played by Martin Donovan.

8
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:18,000
Fred Duggar, played by Nicky Katt.

9
00:53:06,000 --> 00:53:12,000
Rachel Clement, played by Maura Tierney.

10
00:59:00,000 --> 00:59:06,000
Insomnia is a 2002 American neo-noir psychological thriller film directed by Christopher Nolan and written by
Hillary Seitz; it is the only film directed by Nolan that he is not credited with writing.

11
01:04:54,000 --> 01:05:00,000
A remake of the 1997 Norwegian film, it stars Al Pacino, Robin Williams, and Hilary Swank, with
Maura Tierney, Martin Donovan, Nicky Katt, and Paul Dooley in supporting roles.

12
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:54,000
The film follows two Los Angeles homicide detectives
investigating a murder in Nightmute, Alaska.

13
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:48,000
After the killer witnesses an accidental shooting committed by one of the detectives,
they create a plan for both parties to mutually avoid prosecution.

14
01:22:36,000 --> 01:22:42,000
Insomnia premiered at the Tribeca Festival on May 3, 2002, and was
theatrically released in the United States and Canada on May 24, 2002.

15
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:36,000
It grossed $113.8 million worldwide against a production budget of $46 million.

16
01:34:24,000 --> 01:34:30,000
The film received positive reviews, with praise for
Pacino's and Williams's performances.

17
01:40:18,000 --> 01:40:24,000
At the 29th Saturn Awards, Williams was nominated for Best
Supporting Actor, and Seitz was nominated for Best Writing.

18
01:46:12,000 --> 01:46:18,000
The film explores themes of hotel, small town, homicide, confession, blackmail.

19
01:52:06,000 --> 01:52:12,000
The tone is dark and emotional and intense.
